# Workshop, Slopes, And Chests

Consult `README.md` (Core gameplay, Campaign Workshop, Floor height, UI / art style, Agent rules 11–14) and `docs/cave_biome.md` for cave remaps. These are common regression areas.

## Campaign Workshop

- Stamp hover ghosts and preview icons must show **final in-game stamp size** via `CustomLevelStore.stamp_visual_world_rect`.
- **Planks / crystal ledges** (`platform`, `ladder_ledge`) are **160×32** (4 grid cells) — same as campaign `Block` planks. Do not regress to the old half-width **80×24** / 2-cell stamp.
- Multi-cell stamps store the **left** footprint column; `object_world_position` centers on the full footprint.
- **Right-click** removes a stamp on the grid or live preview.
- Stamp grid collapse uses a **▼ / ▶ chevron** (session state: `GameManager.workshop_grid_collapsed`). Do not regress to text-only hide/show labels.
- Do not regress placement ghosts to grid-cell size instead of final stamp size.
- Workshop hub and trail editor chrome use **kid-readable picture icons** (`assets/ui/menu_icon_*.png`, rebuild with `tools/build_workshop_icons.py`) on action buttons (Edit / Add / Remove / Save / Play / Export / Import / ± Length / scroll arrows, etc.). Keep translated labels + tooltips; scroll arrows may be icon-only.
- **Ninja** stamps: live preview sets `NinjaEnemy.editor_marker` so the idle body stays visible at the ambush post. Play / play-test leave `editor_marker` false — dormancy stays fully hidden until ambush. Do not make gameplay ninjas permanently visible.

## Dune slopes

- Under curved desert banks, earth fill must stay dense in the upper wedge (no tile gaps exposing black/sky).
- Keep the warm `FloorSlopeUnderfill` wedge; do not leave featureless voids under the crust.

## Treasure chests

- Gameplay collision height targets **~109% of player height** (`TreasureChest.HEIGHT_RATIO`).
- Do not shrink chests back to old ~95% scale without updating README and tests.
